WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:11.820
14. K2 K2, Chomolangmas or Mount Everest's dangerous

2
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:20.060
little sister, is the highest peak in the Karakoram mountain range of Pakistan. At 8,611

3
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:26.180
meters, it is the second highest mountain in the world. In addition to being the second

4
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:32.420
highest mountain, K2 also has the second highest fatality rate among mountains over

5
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:41.060
8,000 meters. K2 is deadly. It is nicknamed savage mountain because of its fearsome weather.

6
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:48.140
K2 is so dangerous that it has never been climbed in winter. K2 is a rocky mountain

7
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:54.940
up to the 6,000 meter point. After that, it is covered in snow. It rises very steeply

8
00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:01.580
on all sides, making it stand out dramatically in its mountain range. Its steepness, of course,

9
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:09.500
adds to its great difficulty. Anyone attempting to climb K2 must truly climb. This is not a mountain

10
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:16.660
you can hike up. Who has actually climbed K2? Far fewer people than have tried, that's for sure.

11
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:24.420
The first people known to summit, or reach the top of K2, were Lino Lachadeli and Akile Compagnoni.

12
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:33.000
They stood on top of the savage mountain on July 31, 1954. This was the fifth serious attempt to

13
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:40.340
climb the mountain, though teams had been trying since 1902. The next group to summit K2 didn't

14
00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:49.900
make it to the top until August 9, 1977. As of today, 302 people have reached the top of K2.

15
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:58.820
However, 31 of those people died on the descent. A total of 80 people have died trying to climb K2,

16
00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:07.300
meaning that about 26% of those who attempt K2 never make it back. They are killed by avalanches,

17
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:16.140
rockfalls, falling, cold, and exhaustion, or they disappear into snowstorms. Mountain climbing is a

18
00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:22.220
dangerous sport, and K2 is one of its greatest challenges. Despite its cruelty,

19
00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.300
there is something about this great mountain that keeps drawing people to it.
